WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:04.660
Today I'll show you how to design real things, just by describing them, with SOMA AI.

00:05.460 --> 00:07.520
A hand sketch becomes furniture.

00:07.520 --> 00:09.515
A floor plan becomes your flat.

00:09.515 --> 00:11.510
And a robot arm learns to move.

00:14.550 --> 00:19.223
SOMA is a free, open source CAD program with its own AI agent built in.

00:19.223 --> 00:21.000
Download it at somacad.app.

00:22.050 --> 00:23.470
SOMA itself is free.

00:23.470 --> 00:25.954
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

00:25.954 --> 00:28.580
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

00:31.850 --> 00:34.530
You describe what you want, in plain words:

00:34.530 --> 00:37.959
a bookshelf, open at the top, with doors at the bottom.

00:39.293 --> 00:42.037
If anything is unclear, SOMA AI asks first.

00:42.037 --> 00:43.823
You just click your answers.

00:45.296 --> 00:48.386
Then it gets to work, and tells you in plain words what it's doing.

00:51.421 --> 00:54.111
A few minutes later, there's your bookshelf in 3D.

00:57.504 --> 01:02.034
Give it a floor plan and a few photos, and it builds your flat, furnished room by room.

01:09.158 --> 01:12.408
Ask for workshop drawings, with every dimension and a cutting list.

01:16.366 --> 01:17.373
Need it wider?

01:17.373 --> 01:18.380
Drag a slider.

01:18.380 --> 01:21.616
SOMA AI makes the important sizes adjustable.

01:23.223 --> 01:24.858
Hard to put into words?

01:24.858 --> 01:29.193
Draw on the model, send it to SOMA AI, and there's your door.

01:34.544 --> 01:37.061
Will a shelf hold twenty kilos of books?

01:37.061 --> 01:39.074
A strength simulation tells you.

01:40.711 --> 01:43.121
Found an STL that doesn't quite fit?

01:43.121 --> 01:47.205
SOMA AI rebuilds it as an adjustable model, and makes it fit:

01:47.205 --> 01:50.017
here, a desk organizer for business cards.

01:50.872 --> 01:56.202
And when you're happy, export it for your 3D printer, or as a STEP file for any other CAD program.

01:57.272 --> 01:58.590
Sheet metal works too:

01:58.590 --> 02:02.366
a bracket that holds a stepper motor on an aluminium extrusion.

02:02.366 --> 02:05.962
SOMA AI unfolds it into a flat pattern for the laser cutter.

02:09.716 --> 02:14.246
Or a folding steel trestle for the workshop, from steel tube you can cut and weld yourself.

02:15.916 --> 02:20.286
SOMA AI animated how it folds flat, and checked every step for collisions.

02:25.724 --> 02:27.624
It doesn't stop at simple parts.

02:27.624 --> 02:32.494
SOMA AI designed this robot arm, with three stepper motors and a parallel gripper.

02:36.036 --> 02:40.006
It animated the full range of motion, and checked that no part hits another.

02:43.897 --> 02:46.874
Every step SOMA AI takes is saved in the history.

02:46.874 --> 02:49.547
So you can try anything, and always go back.

02:50.797 --> 02:56.972
Built-in skills teach it how to design for 3D printing, CNC milling, sheet metal or the laser cutter.

02:57.897 --> 03:00.421
Already use an agent of your own?

03:00.421 --> 03:05.547
Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode and more work in SOMA too.

03:06.347 --> 03:08.528
It starts in a terminal, right next to your model.

03:10.197 --> 03:12.973
With more time and planning, you can go much further.

03:12.973 --> 03:14.807
All of these were designed in SOMA.

03:17.041 --> 03:21.091
A robot dog, with twelve actuators, each with its own planetary gearbox.

03:22.041 --> 03:24.054
Over two hundred and sixty parts.

03:24.054 --> 03:26.251
Every gear and every screw is there.

03:27.108 --> 03:27.994
And it walks.

03:31.308 --> 03:35.598
A chainsaw, with its two-stroke engine fully modeled, and animated in a cutaway.

03:44.408 --> 03:50.041
A desktop CNC mill, with linear rails and lead screws on all three axes, milling a pattern.

03:52.808 --> 03:57.578
A community member modeled the Kathryn, a Chesapeake Bay skipjack built in 1901.

03:59.808 --> 04:04.658
And a smart speaker, with a fabric cover, several circuit boards and an LED ring.

04:07.458 --> 04:08.622
Here it is, built.

04:14.558 --> 04:16.714
SOMA is free and open source.

04:16.714 --> 04:20.208
Download it at somacad.app, and start building.
